    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Angie Piedrahita",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUhdyR3l38e3FpDZBj9zKTvBUU7TvQrdUjjQqulgsJXaCDYwtwg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "2 months ago",
        "text": "First time to Doya, and I was super impressed! I only wish I could have ordered even more food, but for now, I just know I will be back.\n\nFrom the moment we walked in, the place was fun, exciting, and overall a great ambiance. We did have to have a reservation, and I highly suggest you do too, since it was super busy when we went around 7pm on a weeknight.\n\nThe service was great! Angie was amazing!!! She gave us great recommendations and overall, we  had a great time. We felt taken care of. Food is phenomenal and we will be back!"
      },
      {
        "author": "Nicoly Miyuki",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVn4C0tVKbD2BkMwwjhdYWDRtr28DXBcZByzy1b4OC6XJQNdqu0-w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "a month ago",
        "text": "I always used to drive past Doya and tell myself, 'I have to come here,' and today was finally the day. I'm so glad I did!\n​I absolutely loved this place, from the valet reception to the host, Armando. I didn't have a reservation but decided to just stop by. My husband and I were served by Paul, who was very attentive; he explained the dishes and helped us decide what to order.\n​The drinks are well-crafted and very flavorful. Now, let’s talk about the food—everything is delicious! For starters, I ordered the Truffle Pizza with kasseri, and then the grill board which comes with lamb chops, kebab, and meatballs. Everything is so tasty and really reminds you of Turkey and Greece.\n​I loved the venue, the vibe, and the atmosphere. They have a live DJ from Friday to Sunday, which is really cool. If you are planning to visit Miami and Wynwood, this place absolutely has to be on your bucket list!"
      },
      {
        "author": "Justin Kimura",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVhdZgmjmSsGN40-P3W-lpx_LaB3j4ujIXr-ok7pEAvWpLs0Ad0CQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "3 months ago",
        "text": "Doya, doya, doya. This dinner was by far one of the best Turkish and Greek meze style experiences I’ve had so far! This modern Aegean restaurant in Wynwood sits on a very busy street, so if you're Ubering, I highly recommend getting dropped off a block away and walking. It’s a one way street and traffic can get backed up, especially during dinner service.\n\nThe place itself is an absolute vibe. The energy, music, and atmosphere all made for a fun night out. The service was incredible and our server’s recommendations were spot on as everything we ordered was fantastic. The branzino was easily my favorite dish of the night and one of the best I’ve had.\n\nWe came as a group of six, and this spot is perfect for both small and larger groups. They offer both indoor and outdoor seating, and the party like atmosphere makes it a great place to enjoy drinks, good food and music.\n\nIf you're visiting Miami, you won’t regret coming here. Highly recommend Doya and would definitely come back!"
      }
    ]
