  "Tulum": {
    "placeId": "ChIJcRO1IAC32YgRcwzuRZyQ7n4",
    "address": "485 Brickell Ave, Miami, FL 33131, USA",
    "lat": 25.7686625,
    "lng": -80.188727,
    "rating": 3.6,
    "userRatingsTotal": 56,
    "phone": null,
    "website": "https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/miawm-w-miami/dining/",
    "priceLevel": 3,
    "openingHours": [
      "Monday: 6:30 AM – 8:00 PM",
      "Tuesday: 6:30 AM – 8:00 PM",
      "Wednesday: 6:30 AM – 8:00 PM",
      "Thursday: 6:30 AM – 8:00 PM",
      "Friday: 6:30 AM – 8:00 PM",
      "Saturday: 6:30 AM – 8:00 PM",
      "Sunday: 6:30 AM – 8:00 PM"
    ],
    "mapsUrl": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=9146406894098582643",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Johan Mackie",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUk6szDk-xf5pEV5EhpNaR0xMNI7NPEF19OuERWJ4r9KUkBNfzB=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "3 months ago",
        "text": "Tulum at the W Miami is an absolute gem, and it’s largely because of the exceptional people running the place. From the moment we arrived, Romel, George, and Francisco made us feel genuinely welcomed. Their professionalism and personable approach set the tone for an excellent evening.\nWhat really stood out was their knowledge and care beyond the usual bartending and service. They shared fascinating local history about the area, including details about upcoming development and a construction project on the horizon. They even told us an interesting story about the name of the restaurant and how it came to be, which gave us deeper insight into the place and their passion for what they do. It’s clear they’re invested in their community and genuinely interested in engaging with guests on a deeper level.\n\nThe food is amazing. Everything we had was delicious and perfectly prepared, which made the whole experience even better.\n\nThe atmosphere is perfectly relaxed while maintaining a high level of polish. The views are spectacular, you can see the ocean from the rooftop, and there’s a beautiful church visible from the bar area, which adds to the character of the space. Everything was impeccably clean and well maintained.\n\nWhat really impressed me was how Romel, George, and Francisco treated my daughter. As a kind gesture, they even treated her to a virgin drink. They made her feel valued and welcomed throughout the visit, just like they did with us. That kind of genuine hospitality speaks volumes about a place.\n\nThe staff here are true gems who clearly represent the best of the best. They know exactly how to treat people well and make you want to come back. I’ll absolutely be returning, and I’d recommend Tulum to anyone looking for great drinks, amazing food, incredible views, and most importantly, authentic hospitality from people who genuinely care.​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​"
      },
      {
        "author": "anthony sarnataro",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjX0gtwhUCd__CwOJMQglNHq3dhK6p6eYj0e8B2IxUiByDoc5To=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "a year ago",
        "text": "SoulEdge: Back in the Game\nArrived in late April. When I arrived there was a private event. Fernando went out of his way to help me out with seating. I ate outside and enjoying the breeze. Jorge my server gave me excellent service, along with the other lady server. I ate a Tulum Beast Burger 8 oz. Blend of bison, elk, wild boar, and wagyu beef, grilled queso fresco, demi-glace mushrooms  dressed arugula salad, pickled red onion, tomato jam. And Lava Cake w/melted marshmallows. Nice touch the quesco fresco and sweet tomato jam compliment each other. Visit dedicated to my then ex German American girlfriend who looks like Lagertha from a vikings tv show. Cue in the songs Back in the Game\nSong by Airbourne ‧ 2013 and Let Me Go\nSong by Avril Lavigne. 🇺🇸🇩🇪🎸🙏✌️"
      },
      {
        "author": "Anthony Sarnataro",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUOiWxikJEqtzFuCGyWYId7R-iGPkN0L4jN639SxDFJbcn_Tk0=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "a year ago",
        "text": "SoulEdge: Makes you feel, She's One of a Kind.\nThis review is based from breakfast & lunch visits. Tulum located where ADDiKT Modern Kitchen used to be. Jessica my server gave me excellent service. I ordered Tulum Benedict, Haas Avocado Pureé, Pico de Gallo, Spiced Pepitas, Poached Pasture-Raised Eggs, Housemade Hollandaise on a English Muffin. Another dish of Scramble Eggs , Chicken Sausage, bread. Smooth silk butter. Dine for Lunch (young white Hispanic front desk lady with curly hair helped me get the elevator) I ate Tulum Flatbread, the dish (not that spicy, my 1st try) has Marinated Pineapple, Jalapeno, Hot Honey, with Steak and Warm Ocho Rios Bread Pudding, good touch on the ice cream. Panther Coffee (inside hotel Lobby) has good coffee. Visit dedicated to my then German American ex girlfriend, who looks like Lagertha from a vikings tv show. And she's a Maddona fan. Cue in songs: Don't Tell Me & Crazy for You, both sung by Maddona. 🇺🇸🇩🇪🎸🙏"
      }
    ]
  },
