  "The Amalfi LLama": {
    "placeId": "ChIJB172iFis2YgRp4-Ajb6DPpY",
    "address": "19505 Biscayne Blvd Building D, Suite 4150, Miami, FL 33180, USA",
    "lat": 25.9547616,
    "lng": -80.1430431,
    "rating": 4.7,
    "userRatingsTotal": 2381,
    "phone": "(305) 726-0226",
    "website": "https://www.amalfillama.com/",
    "priceLevel": 4,
    "openingHours": [
      "Monday: 4:00 – 10:00 PM",
      "Tuesday: 4:00 – 10:00 PM",
      "Wednesday: 4:00 – 10:00 PM",
      "Thursday: 4:00 – 10:00 PM",
      "Friday: 4:00 PM – 12:00 AM",
      "Saturday: 11:30 AM – 12:00 AM",
      "Sunday: 11:30 AM – 10:00 PM"
    ],
    "mapsUrl": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=10826235408686288807",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Michael M",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU5PG-_AznLrtYufD_G7OTLdlNAkTaeHkcaDkGdBmeKHibu5rg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 4,
        "relativeTime": "a month ago",
        "text": "We went to The Amalfi Llama for lunch, so it wasn’t very busy, and the atmosphere was absolutely top-tier. The decor is beautiful, the music is great and our waiter gave us excellent service.\n\nWhile everything was good, the food overall was just \"okay\" for the price tag. When you spend this much, you expect the meal to be memorable and the main dishes didn't hit the mark.\n\nThe Starters & Sides: The starters were pretty good. The crab cakes and the pizza were both decent but nothing crazy.\n\nFor the sides, the asparagus was excellent and the French fries were just alright, nothing to write home about. The lobster gnocchi side was also a bit of a disappointment.\n\nThe Mains: This is where we were let down. The ribeye steak didn't impress me at all and the hamburger just wasn't good enough for the price.\n\nThe Highlight: Do not skip the butter cake! It was absolutely amazing, delicious and honestly mind-blowing. The high price tag is 100% justified for that dessert.\n\nGo for the amazing vibes, great service and the butter cake but don't expect the food to blow you away for the money."
      },
      {
        "author": "Flavia Salzano",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXsOsyYnqHzof0daCY0ffpCu5qPMAUEWatKU4bysywoHRQdSS1A=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 3,
        "relativeTime": "3 months ago",
        "text": "If you’re walking around the outdoor dining area at Aventura Mall, this spot definitely catches your eye , beautiful setting, great ambiance, and that inviting wood-fire concept.\nWe started with a crab cake, it was delicious, then shared a Prime Rib, tender overall, but with some chewy sections, French fries were just ok, and a Positano pizza, which is more of a very thin flatbread with pepperoni and slightly spicy peppers. We ordered a Peroni and a non-alcoholic beer.\n\nThe food? Good.\nThe experience? Nice.\nBut here’s the honest part…\n\nFor what we ordered, essentially one starter, one main, a flatbread and 2 beers and 1 Acqua Panna, the bill came out to $238 (tip included)\nAnd that’s where it loses me.❌\nThe place is undeniably pretty, but the food didn’t feel special enough to justify that price point. You can easily find restaurants in Miami where you eat twice as much, with the same (or better or more realistic Italian ) quality, for significantly less.\nService was great!\nWould I go back? Probably not, not for that value.\n\n✨ My take:\nGo for the ambiance, maybe a drink at the beautiful bar they have, but if you’re looking for a memorable food experience, there are stronger options in this price range.\n\nWhen you go… tell them Flavia Sent You 😉"
      },
      {
        "author": "Yeimar",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocItk2ZfRmZe_HlYrZgPT1vlsmrKjUNKwmyeeOdAdQE8l-Y_Ww=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "8 months ago",
        "text": "I absolutely loved the place; it's beautiful, elegant, and comfortable all at once. I was thrilled with my Smoke and Tallow drink, and something really special was that since I don't eat cheese, Chef Val came to my table to suggest a cheese-free option. That was exceptional—the service and kindness were outstanding. At the end, he came back to ask if I enjoyed it and how I felt. I can't forget the dessert; it was fantastic, especially since I'm obsessed with passion fruit. I highly recommend the warm butter cake.\n\nAnd what truly sets it apart, besides the exquisite food, is the service. Melissa gave us 100% outstanding service. She made our dinner even more special with her recommendations, her hospitality, and her positive energy. I definitely loved it. See you soon!"
      }
    ]
  },
