        "text": "Paperfish Miami is honestly one of my favorite hidden spots in Brickell. The food is always fresh and consistently delicious, and in my opinion, it’s not expensive at all for the quality you get. The vibe is super cute and laid-back—nothing overly fancy, which makes it perfect for a casual but still nice night out. They offer happy hour, lunch menu, valet parking for $15, or you can easily find street parking nearby and take a short walk to the restaurant. Definitely a go-to spot for me.\n\nWe ordered:\n-crispy rice (salmon and tuna)\n-tiradito apassionado\n-rock shrimp tempura\n-pork and shrimp dumplings\n-acevichado roll\n-misuna roll"
