  "Baires Grill Brickell": {
    "placeId": "ChIJwzbGDoS22YgR0yi7vExudM0",
    "address": "1010 S Miami Ave, Miami, FL 33130, USA",
    "lat": 25.7640139,
    "lng": -80.193375,
    "rating": 4.6,
    "userRatingsTotal": 3026,
    "phone": "(786) 580-4923",
    "website": "https://www.bairesgrill.com/",
    "priceLevel": null,
    "openingHours": [
      "Monday: 11:30 AM – 11:00 PM",
      "Tuesday: 11:30 AM – 11:00 PM",
      "Wednesday: 11:30 AM – 11:00 PM",
      "Thursday: 11:30 AM – 11:00 PM",
      "Friday: 11:30 AM – 11:30 PM",
      "Saturday: 12:00 – 11:30 PM",
      "Sunday: 12:00 – 11:00 PM"
    ],
    "mapsUrl": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=14804579150936615123",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Nestor Rodriguez",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIW3r85NaRTbx9dd7EdEpeYGj79NROPL-eeLi2_LcaIPJMbGA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 2,
        "relativeTime": "3 months ago",
        "text": "Food was solid—not exceptional, but well-executed. The space is genuinely beautiful with great outdoor seating and ambiance. That’s where the positives end.\nService was inconsistent and frustrating. After finishing, we waited with dirty plates on the table for an extended period because our server disappeared. I understand shifts change, but that’s no excuse for leaving customers hanging. More problematic: I was charged for a side salad without being informed it wasn’t included in my order. That feels like deliberate misdirection to inflate the bill—exactly the kind of tactic that erodes trust. If they have to resort to that, there’s a real problem with how they operate.\nThe service issues and the hidden charges weren’t oversights. They suggest either carelessness or intentional practice. Either way, it doesn’t inspire confidence. Beautiful restaurant, disappointing execution"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mauro Deffendini",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLH1-Qxz4Kd23rXnxkA9xtwEU2cyTR4gR3fcsMmAASESGAQbQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 4,
        "relativeTime": "6 months ago",
        "text": "Dinner at Baires Grill was a fantastic experience, made even more special thanks to Matilde, our server. She thoughtfully addressed every request, from warming up the bread to perfectly toasting it, small details that truly elevated the evening.\n\nThe appetizers set the tone.. A must-try is the goat cheese cheese cake: creamy, smooth, flavorful, and slightly sweet. If you enjoy a sweet-forward appetizer, this one is a winner. However, if you’re leaning more savory, La Tablita is the way to go, juicy blood sausage, meaty and flavorful sausage, and cheese-onion empanadas that are perfectly grilled cheese and wonderfully toasted. Another standout was the grilled octopus with crushed almonds, cooked just right and full of depth.\n\nFor the entrées, you can’t go wrong with the Brazilian-style picanha cooked the Argentine way, rich, juicy, and full of flavor. The classic filet mignon was also very meaty, though I found it slightly mild; pairing it with the sweet potato fries was the best match, they were unexpectedly better than the truffle fries.\n\nThe desserts also stole the show. The molten dulce de leche lava cake, the crêpe with warm dulce de leche, and the flan were our full dose of dulce de leche. The highlight was the lava cake served warmed, melting the ice cream and bathing the dessert in vanilla lava ice cream. The warm dulce de leche on the crêpe felt like an extra shot of one of my favorite Argentine treats. We wrapped it all up with a warm, foamy cinnamon cappuccino, the perfect digestivo.\n\nPro tip: make sure to order a good Malbec or Cabernet Sauvignon (of course Argentinian wines) to properly accompany the meats.\n\nThe ambiance is very corporate steakhouse oriented, maybe it is the Brickell vibes.\n\nSide note: love the name, Baires, short for Buenos Aires, a very creative acronym.  🇦🇷"
      },
      {
        "author": "Trisha Bernardin",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWtcBEtjgq22eVZ9SvjU39gNvQQb7gRaY7Z504-iZHW7p9Heyyo=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 3,
        "relativeTime": "2 months ago",
        "text": "CONFIT AND GRILLED OCTOPUS\nGood char on the octopus, zero salt in the dish itself\n\nTABLITA BAIRES\nNot bad, but not for me. Sweetbread is thymus or pancreas of veal or lambs.\nSausage was extremely greasy.\nEmpanada was satisfactory.\n\nFrench onion soup\nSalty\n\nPicanha\nFat was not rendered down, steak was very chewy; not properly rested. Also no salt.\n\nMashed potatoes\nExtremely watery, tasted almost like boxed mashed potatoes. Very little to no salt.\n\nBAIRES STEAK\nSteak was over salted but dish overall was very good. Avocados, tomatoes, and lettuce were all fresh.\n\nAtmosphere was great; the decor was beautiful, there was live music, our wait staff were very quick and friendly."
      }
    ]
  },
