  "Le Specialita Café & Market": {
    "placeId": "ChIJDYJ34TG32YgRL6OSt-0n5ss",
    "address": "2653 S Bayshore Dr, Miami, FL 33133, USA",
    "lat": 25.7307663,
    "lng": -80.2359199,
    "rating": 4.6,
    "userRatingsTotal": 56,
    "phone": "(305) 677-0621",
    "website": "https://lespecialitacoconutgrove.com/",
    "priceLevel": 2,
    "openingHours": [
      "Monday: 8:00 AM – 9:00 PM",
      "Tuesday: 8:00 AM – 9:00 PM",
      "Wednesday: 8:00 AM – 9:00 PM",
      "Thursday: 8:00 AM – 9:00 PM",
      "Friday: 8:00 AM – 10:00 PM",
      "Saturday: 8:00 AM – 10:00 PM",
      "Sunday: 8:00 AM – 9:00 PM"
    ],
    "mapsUrl": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=14692474736283394863",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Alberto Rodriguez",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJ9pxlrKVR3vRz5l-X8PwgJuwhGSlFvOOPtuJx9CE6zS-_hVA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "4 months ago",
        "text": "Writing\nI visited La Especialice in Coconut Grove with my wife and our dog for a late lunch/early dinner, and overall it was a great experience. The place is beautiful, very well decorated, and has a really inviting atmosphere. The menu is quite diverse, offering plenty of options, and the food was very good. Prices felt reasonable for the quality and location.\nOur only complaint was that the service was noticeably slow compared to other tables around us. That said, setting that aside and considering everything else, we would definitely come back."
      },
      {
        "author": "Francesca Hemmerde",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIDH3JrCyjMTffLOj5MwigE2Aoe0xI5l3ll6L8t3V8bMAdAvA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "4 months ago",
        "text": "⸻\n\nFirst, to set expectations: this is not the same La Specialità pizza place from Milan, and as far as I can tell it has no connection to it—so yes, it’s a bit funny that they share the same name.\n\nThis location is part of the Cipriani / Bellini / Mr. C family, and the quality reflects that. It’s casual, welcoming, and very convenient for anyone living around Coconut Grove.\n\nThey open early in the morning, making it a perfect place to grab breakfast or stop by for a quick coffee. We had breakfast there and loved it. The food felt authentically Italian, simple and delicious, and the service was excellent.\n\nWhat I enjoyed most is that it really feels like a neighborhood Italian spot—the kind of place where you can pop in for a quick espresso, maybe grab a cookie or a pastry, and continue your day. I actually stopped by right after the gym once, which shows how easy and relaxed the atmosphere is.\n\nAnother great feature is that you can also buy prepared food to take home, like classic Italian meatballs and other ready-to-eat dishes. On the second floor there’s also a market with excellent Italian products, something that has been missing in the Grove.\n\nThey even have gelato, which I’m really looking forward to trying next time.\n\nIf you live in Coconut Grove, it’s definitely worth stopping by—whether for breakfast, coffee, or to pick up some great Italian products for home."
      },
      {
        "author": "patricia oliver",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVlXbzyDTJBuozB33bj27TJfoljxqc3r6TYOO095ODh5PfEETg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "4 months ago",
        "text": "Le Especialita by the renowned Cipriani Group, delivers a truly exceptional Italian experience in Miami.\n\nOne of the highlights is their beautifully curated market, offering a fantastic selection of Italian delicatessen and top-quality products perfect for anyone who appreciates authentic Italian cuisine and lifestyle.\n\nI visited for lunch and everything was impeccable. The appetizers, especially the Carciofi alla Romana and Arancini, were delicious. The pizzas particularly the pizza tower with three different varieties were outstanding. The pasta was equally excellent, fresh and full of flavor.\n\nService, quality, and atmosphere all reflect the classic Cipriani standard of elegance and consistency.\n\nHighly recommended. Looking forward to coming back."
      }
    ]
  },
