        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "5 months ago",
        "text": "I was very satisfied with my entire experience.\nI actually found this place by accident. I drove by one day, noticed a crowd outside, and that’s always a good sign when I’m trying a new restaurant. If you drive by too fast, you might miss it because it’s a bit hidden, but it’s absolutely worth stopping for.\n\nThe staff is extremely friendly and attentive, and they offer a great selection of wines and food.\n\nI went for brunch and ordered the Short Rib Benedict. The dish was spectacular—the meat was incredibly tender and full of flavor. The salmon was also delicious and perfectly seasoned.\n\nFor dessert, I tried the Pistachio Cheesecake. It came covered in pistachio sauce and dried fruits, giving every bite a perfect crunchy contrast. The portion is generous—definitely enough for two people.\n\nI’m already planning to come back to try the regular menu.\nSee you all again soon."
