  "A Fish Called Avalon": {
    "placeId": "ChIJbQDyqJK02YgR6kKjr7ipYiA",
    "address": "700 Ocean Dr, Miami Beach, FL 33139, USA",
    "lat": 25.7768927,
    "lng": -80.13153899999999,
    "rating": 4.6,
    "userRatingsTotal": 1555,
    "phone": "(305) 532-1727",
    "website": "http://afishcalledavalon.com/",
    "priceLevel": 3,
    "openingHours": [
      "Monday: 5:00 – 10:30 PM",
      "Tuesday: 5:00 – 10:30 PM",
      "Wednesday: 5:00 – 10:30 PM",
      "Thursday: 5:00 – 11:00 PM",
      "Friday: 5:00 – 11:00 PM",
      "Saturday: 5:00 – 11:00 PM",
      "Sunday: 5:00 – 10:00 PM"
    ],
    "mapsUrl": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=2333614167617127146",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "allyson bozzello",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLg3T1JjK74pAFPe9pwKjxBF0DngaSkWISWa-IaHqof8BTlCg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "2 months ago",
        "text": "We didn’t come to Miami Beach for fun in the sun. We were there because of a family emergency and ended up staying for 10 nights out of which 6 nights were at the Avalon\n\nThe staff embraced us like family. They were genuinely concerned about our situation, offered prayers, and provided comfort during a very difficult time.\n\nFrom the owner, Michelle, to the staff members Alejandro, Rosario, Vargas, Camille, and Julio, we always felt safe, supported, and cared for. My husband had to leave before I did, but he felt completely at ease knowing I was in good hands. They truly watched over me.\n\nThe people at Avalon are amazing. The hotel is wonderful and the food is excellent!!!! I can’t even pick a favorite dish as they were all delightful. The escargot, oysters, and octopus were our favorite appetizers.  The twin lobster dinner and the macadamia encrusted snapper were phenomenal. Hands down best Eggs Benedict!! We will never forget the kindness and compassion they showed us ( and the full bellies)"
      },
      {
        "author": "Philip Figueroa",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKx8B3yBk3H-Vg0jRxaK2CDfuqtLqXVFKxbJ26VBoOfP5mcUg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 4,
        "relativeTime": "4 months ago",
        "text": "Really good restaurant. We came for an earlier dinner and happy hour. We felt the happy hour menu had better appetizer offerings than the normal menu.\n\nFrom the happy hour menu we got spanakopita, mussels, and shrimp tacos.  HH drinks got the twisted lychee and MARACUYĂ. The drinks were a little too sweet for my liking but good offerings. The HH plates were very good especially the shrimp tacos and mussels. We got extra bread to eat up all the sauce.\n\nFrom the full menu we got the bang bang shrimp (not the best for the price) and entree we got the braised black grouper and macadamia crusted snapper which were both really good.\n\nDefinitely recommend the HH for appetizers and drinks and then get entrees. The Live music also enhanced the vibe and experience"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mandy",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWWxEKXBKLzVaYB5S7_M_NBRBIJa1lxcH0vl0x1tcCJzce98olChA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "6 months ago",
        "text": "Had a wonderful dinner!! I literally just got into town to celebrate my solo birthday weekend and needed some dinner. After walking Ocean Ave. I decided on eating here and so glad I did. Richard was my server and he made my 1st meal in town amazing. I had the bang bang shrimp app, the citrus chicken for my meal and the coconut creme brulee for dessert all absolutely delicious. Oh and my drink was the 1941. Richard was so amazing that in talking he learned I was in town to celebrate my bday and when he brought my dessert I was surprised with servers and the live artist singing me Happy birthday and a candle in my brulee that I got to blow out. Talk about making a guest feel special!! 5 stars! Thank you for such a wonderful evening!!"
      }
    ]
  },
