        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "3 months ago",
        "text": "Very impressed by this new restaurant concept. The decor and ambiance are what this area needed -a  cool, intimate spot with a  well-curated menu. My congratulations on your new spot, you’ve done a great job. Love the street-style camera TVs before getting to the main entrance. Really caught our attention, and the view of the kitchen from the outside brings curiosity.\n\nThe food was very delicious. I’m not surprised because the food was great at Paya as well, but this is something different and elevated.\n\nWe went with the scallop crudo, which was a burst of flavors. I loved it! The duck bao buns were spectacular— juicy and cooked to perfection. We also ordered the pork ribs, which were really good, but I think they can be slow-cooked a little more for that fall-off-the-bone effect, but I’m no chef, lol . Lastly, that Indonesian rice was something new for me, and it was really good!\n\nShout out to Fernando; he recommended every single dish and did a great job.  Overall, it was a great experience, and as a local, I will be back."
