  "Amazonia Nikkei": {
    "placeId": "ChIJLx-9Mail2YgRBpMb54ouUiQ",
    "address": "6704 Main St, Miami Lakes, FL 33014, USA",
    "lat": 25.9130572,
    "lng": -80.30979169999999,
    "rating": 4.9,
    "userRatingsTotal": 1379,
    "phone": "(305) 323-0573",
    "website": "https://amazonianikkei.com/",
    "priceLevel": 2,
    "openingHours": [
      "Monday: 12:00 – 10:00 PM",
      "Tuesday: 12:00 – 10:00 PM",
      "Wednesday: 12:00 – 10:00 PM",
      "Thursday: 12:00 – 10:00 PM",
      "Friday: 12:00 – 11:00 PM",
      "Saturday: 12:00 – 11:00 PM",
      "Sunday: 12:00 – 10:00 PM"
    ],
    "mapsUrl": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=2617205507573388038",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Eric Gutierrez",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKjdfTZUNeCZswFSpPKQNAH5GFqJRcBFrxYnXoqYTNgyNt-Ew=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "3 months ago",
        "text": "Absolutely outstanding experience. This place truly nails the Japanese fusion concept, every dish felt creative, balanced, and executed at a very high level. From the beautifully presented sushi with rich, layered flavors to the perfectly cooked meats, everything was on point. You can tell there’s real attention to detail in both technique and presentation.\n\nThe ambiance is elegant yet relaxed, making it perfect for both a casual night out or a special occasion. Service was equally impressive—attentive without being intrusive.\n\nSpecial thanks to Matias, who made the experience even better with his professionalism, great recommendations, and genuine hospitality. He really elevated the night.\n\nHighly recommend this is a spot in Miami Lakes. I’ll definitely be coming back to."
      },
      {
        "author": "Santiago Bolivar",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUGkvhdxKNh8wVPcBVDSeH8caz3_ZBtU_12pBdWr8lvXMhZrr6L=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "7 months ago",
        "text": "This is a wonderful Gem found in Miami lakes. They offer a very  unique fusion of Peruvian and Japanese cuisine, with fresh ingredients that will leave your palate so satisfied.\n\nWe went there for my wife’s birthday, parking is a little tight because they’re located in a shopping center that even though has lots of parking it’s packed. Decorated with Christmas lights perfect spot for the family.\n\nOur server was Matias, amazing service and on point with all order and recommendations.\n\nWe had:\n\nGyozas guancaina: we had to order two because the first ones were gone in a minute. Amazing must order\n\nMagurno acevichado: the freshness of the fish was insane. Perfect balance of flavors\n\nSake chatsune: deliciousness  in a roll\n\nFor dessert we had profiteroles with matcha icecream. It’s not on the menu but ask for it!\n\nCocktails were on point. Not your regular cocktail.. very well elaborated.\n\nMusic was perfect volume and genre super enjoyable whilendining. Perfect for a date night or a fancy family night. They accommodated with a high chair we had requested and it was ready waiting for us.\n\nWe were seated immediately but we had a reservation so notate that"
      },
      {
        "author": "Brandi M.",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWuwqTwbovq9btGmhfpi9k3iGHNnt8yUHdNzgaGjBcOGoAYoVr7uQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "2 months ago",
        "text": "We saw Peruvian Japanese and had to stop.\nFelt a little bad with how causally dressed I came in for lunch on the spur of the moment because this restaurant is so beautiful inside.\nWe got 4 items. Tuna crispy rice, The lomo dumplings. A wagyu sushi roll and made our main course the miso butter pork loin.\nThe lomo dumplings were good, but to me they didn't embody lomo saltado. They just tasted like ground beef dumplings. Still very good.\nThe sushi roll was fantastic. Very very good. I loved everything about it. Crispy. Savory. Fresh. Very good. I really loved our tuna crispy rice as well, but Moving on to the star of the show. That miso pork loin. I won't lie. I've had much more tender pork loin. And it sounds silly. But the best part of the dish wasn't even the pork in our opinion. It was the caramelized onions. Both of us said they were the best we had ever had and they elevated the dish to a whole other level.  I wish I could put them on everything.\nAnother little complementary item they had us try was literally just a piece of sweet potato in this yellow sauce. Both of us were very impressed with that too. I would have ordered a whole side of those sweet potatoes.\nReally enjoyed my meal here.\nGreat good. Great service and lovely ambiance."
      }
    ]
  },
