        "relativeTime": "a week ago",
        "text": "Dining at 1910 was an unforgettable experience. The restaurant’s name immediately brought back memories of the iconic restaurant in my hometown in Cuba, and it felt like a beautiful tribute or representation of it.\n\nThe ambiance is elegant, classy, and inviting, creating the perfect atmosphere for a special meal. Every dish we ordered was absolutely delicious. My husband had the lobster soup  and it was truly top-notch. We also had  the grilled octopus, which was perfectly cooked, incredibly flavorful, and served in a very generous portion.\n\nTo make the experience even better, our waitress, Ismar (I hope I got her name right), was warm, attentive, and provided outstanding service throughout our meal.\n\nWe left thoroughly impressed and are already planning to return very soon. Highly recommended!"
