  "Maison Ostrow": {
    "placeId": "ChIJSeE1l9uz2YgRxZY0cKBMT9c",
    "address": "1666 79th Street Causeway Ste 102, North Bay Village, FL 33141, USA",
    "lat": 25.8483949,
    "lng": -80.1510568,
    "rating": 4.8,
    "userRatingsTotal": 233,
    "phone": "(786) 803-8092",
    "website": "https://www.maisonostrow.com/",
    "priceLevel": 4,
    "openingHours": [
      "Monday: 11:00 AM – 11:30 PM",
      "Tuesday: 11:30 AM – 11:30 PM",
      "Wednesday: 11:30 AM – 11:30 PM",
      "Thursday: 11:30 AM – 11:30 PM",
      "Friday: Closed",
      "Saturday: Closed",
      "Sunday: 11:00 AM – 11:30 PM"
    ],
    "mapsUrl": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=15514703493275621061",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Rich Herrera",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW2uazg42wwcUCMIhZnKPCAE2DAgg74qT2yorXEGCb8dHXWWrJeMg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "a month ago",
        "text": "About 18 months ago, Chef Olivia Ostrow joined me on my podcast. I told her if I ever made it to Miami, I’d visit her restaurant. This week, I finally kept that promise.\n\nMaison Ostrow is a charming French-inspired restaurant serving elevated kosher cuisine. We started with rich duck rillettes and fresh baguette, then moved on to a fantastic lamb ragu cavatelli with tender braised lamb and homemade pasta that soaked up every drop of rosemary jus.\n\nMy wife’s steak frites was cooked perfectly, and the hand-cut fries were impossible to stop stealing. Dessert was a tableside rum pineapple flambé with vanilla ice cream and caramel sauce, a sweet and memorable ending to a great meal.\n\nThe food was excellent, but the hospitality was even better.\n\n⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nA little slice of France in Miami, and absolutely worth the visit."
      },
      {
        "author": "BobnMiami",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUejdLIwK8Z8eU_zNJSvLR_Darn1G0irh7O3TA-wuehCad8haI=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "3 months ago",
        "text": "We returned to this wonderfully exquisite French restaurant in its new location and thoroughly enjoyed everything and every moment!  Each dish is presented beautifully in French tradition, and with creativity using all kosher ingredients but somehow taste like dairy items, whether it is cheese on a smoked trout Ceasar Salad, which was amazing, or a bone marrow butter sauce that doesn't use real butter, or the vanilla ice cream that is on top of a delicious apple tart!  I have to mention the incredibly dedicated wait staff. Gonzalo was our waiter, and whether it was his efforts to find the wine of our liking, or making certain that our glasses were full, or his description of each item on the menu, he made our experience even more enjoyable!  Eyal, the manager also checked in with us, and he explained a number of new things that the new location has, such as a full service bar, a beautiful private room, a larger kitchen giving the ability to create more wonderful dishes. They have a great list of kosher wines as well. Whether you keep kosher or not, dining at Maison Ostrow is an exceptional dining experience!!"
      },
      {
        "author": "M F",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIlw4wc1l4enCiHbXU0i78IKKeotg5Uu8DDDklMLvpulmQnkg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "7 months ago",
        "text": "I was transported to Paris tonight. Authentic French food. Amazing ambience. The staff were beyond attentive and plentiful. Beautiful live music. What a perfect little gem here in Miami. I’m so glad we tried this beautiful French restaurant out - we flew from australia for a few days so handpicked the best reviewed restaurants. Maison Ostrow didn’t disappoint!"
      }
    ]
  },
