  "Morton's The Steakhouse - North Miami Beach": {
    "placeId": "ChIJhzuxE6yt2YgRPdaUjNsY22k",
    "address": "17399 Biscayne Blvd, Miami, FL 33160, USA",
    "lat": 25.9367875,
    "lng": -80.1489765,
    "rating": 4.4,
    "userRatingsTotal": 1365,
    "phone": "(305) 945-3131",
    "website": "https://www.mortons.com/location/mortons-the-steakhouse-north-miami-beach-fl/",
    "priceLevel": 4,
    "openingHours": [
      "Monday: 5:00 – 9:00 PM",
      "Tuesday: 5:00 – 9:00 PM",
      "Wednesday: 5:00 – 9:00 PM",
      "Thursday: 5:00 – 9:00 PM",
      "Friday: 4:00 – 10:00 PM",
      "Saturday: 4:00 – 10:00 PM",
      "Sunday: 4:00 – 9:00 PM"
    ],
    "mapsUrl": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=7627717725117535805",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Angie Uribe",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLEJLkmgCoSZ_nmf4AKXqsLFuXBFMdml-1T0uPp-D7NgzVM2A=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2",
        "rating": 4,
        "relativeTime": "3 months ago",
        "text": "I recently dined at Morton’s The Steakhouse and overall had a good experience, but it didn’t quite match the level I expected for the price point.\n\nThe food itself was enjoyable. We ordered the wagyu beef dumplings, a NY strip, and an aged ribeye, along with a bottle of red wine and two martinis. Everything was well-prepared and flavorful, and our server was kind, personable, and attentive throughout the meal.\n\nWhere the experience fell short for me was in the overall service details and ambiance. When dining at a restaurant in this category, I expect a more elevated, seamless experience from start to finish. Small touches make a big difference. Bread should come pre-sliced without needing to ask, wine service should feel more polished, and table maintenance should be more consistent throughout the meal. These are subtle things, but they stand out, especially with a hospitality background.\n\nThe ambiance also didn’t fully reflect the premium pricing. It felt more standard than elevated, which made the overall experience feel slightly mismatched compared to expectations.\n\nOverall, it was a solid dinner with good food and a friendly server, but not quite the top-tier experience I anticipated for a restaurant at this level. I will return and hope for a better experience."
      },
      {
        "author": "Leidi Chavez",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWBZdYZRbphcNILdz4BXjtp1H_WDThonTkieIDiSdT0GyyvMM1JyQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "11 months ago",
        "text": "This place is excellent. The manager was the one who sat us and he was so welcoming and accommodating especially since I had my baby and toddler with me and I had some specific requests.\nNow, our server Dan was great, so nice, patient, and attentive, plus all his recommendations were on point. Service was excellent.\nAll the food we ordered came out very good and very tasty. Those steaks were without doubt excellent. The desserts were so delicious, especially the key lime pie. Yum!\nWe also interacted with other staff members and I have to say they were all very nice. Alfonso was friendly and funny and made us laugh so much."
      },
      {
        "author": "Shula R",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVMWIQOq1ietpOApzokz00aKM5IX1n8d_LXURcTityOXPtAnE5s=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6",
        "rating": 4,
        "relativeTime": "8 months ago",
        "text": "Located between Aventura, North Miami Beach and Sunny Isles this Morton’s is definitely reminiscent of an older (not that old but the vibe) classic steak house. We came for Thanksgiving dinner and had reservations which was helpful as the restaurant was packed in the front room which is usually all they use for nightly service. We were placed in the back room which is normally used for private functions. They were serving their regular menu as well as a special 4 course turkey meal for $69.\n\nOur server started out pretty attentive and while we needed a bit to initially order, she checked on us periodically until we were ready. Food and beverage took a little longer than usual for a restaurant like this but not extreme. Unfortunately though after a certain point, our server became harder and harder to find. There was no checking back to see if we needed more water and once we were done with dessert, it took about 30 minutes to get and pay for our check.\n\nNow for the main event, the food. The complimentary bread was good but perhaps could have been sliced prior to bringing to table so everyone’s hands at the table don’t need to be on it to get a slice. Bar drinks were smooth and delicious. The wedge salad was pretty solid! We opted for a mix of traditional turkey, fish, and of course steak. The soup and salad portions were fairly small but tasty. The main course was filing and flavorful but not a ton of turkey. The pecan streusel cheesecake was delightful and I’d definitely eat that if it were just on the menu in general. The ribeye was perfectly cooked and tasted great as expected but presentation (since it doesn’t come with anything for $70) was a little lackluster. The miso sea bass was amazingly flavorful and delicate all at the same time. Would definitely recommend this if you are here but don’t eat steak."
      }
    ]
  },
